Description: spec-first LaTeX document compiler
 folio compiles LaTeX documents to PDF with its own consistent
 semantics; it is written from scratch in Rust.
 .
 This package is self-contained and needs no TeX Live: it ships
 folio's curated data tree in /usr/share/folio/texmf (Computer
 Modern, AMS, Latin Modern, the EC metrics with the common cm-super
 shapes, URW Times/Helvetica/Courier, hyphenation patterns for twelve
 languages and the standard BibTeX styles).
 .
 An installed TeX Live, if any, is used for files the data tree does
 not have, and enables the slimtex fallback engine.

